{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1097281-lore-of-the-flesh","id":1097281,"title":"Lore of the Flesh","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-26T13:55:17-07:00","id":1097281,"title":"Lore of the Flesh","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>** Manipulate Nerves</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Like Body Control, this evocation allows the demon to manipulate a subject\u2019s nervous system. Strength and reflexes can be enhanced, senses can be dulled or sharpened, or the person can </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">be </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">subjected to waves of intense pleasure or pain. </span></span><br /> <b>System:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"> Roll Intelligence </span></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">+ </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Medicine. The difficulty is determined </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">by </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">the complexity of the intended effect. Reducing the effects of pain is difficulty 6, while increasing the speed of a person\u2019s reflexes (increasing his Dexterity) is </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">7 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">or </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">8. </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Sharpening a person\u2019s senses (or dulling them) might require a difficulty of 9 or more. Each success increases or decreases a relevant physical trait or wound penalty </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">by </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">one, as appropriate for the effort. The effects of this evocation last for the duration of the scene. To perform this evocation on another individual, the demon must be able to make physical contact, and a resisted Willpower (difficulty 8) can be made to counteract your character\u2019s effort. </span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#686868\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">So basically, with this you could reduce wound penalties(1 per success) or increase and decrease Dexterity. or sharpen and dull senses, what about Strength ? it mentions Strength in the description but not in the system, does this power cover strength aswell ? if that's the case, that kinda trumps the physical edge of the rank 3 power(leaving aside the mental attributes that can be risen). so can it or not ?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#686868\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">and how exactly would the effects be if i decide to dull someone's senses ? does it basically reduce perception trait by 1 per success ? or ?</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#686868\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">next, if i decide to pump a friend's attributes, and he's not willing to resist. does that negate the need for that resistance willpowe roll ?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#686868\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Are the powers of this lore considered reflexive to activate ?</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> *** Manipulate Flesh </div> </div> </div></b><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">This evocation allows the demon to manipulate a subject\u2019s physical form (be it her own or another\u2019s), adding muscle mass, increasing bone density or expanding mental faculties. </span></span><br /> <b>System:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"> Roll Intelligence </span></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">+ </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Medicine. Each success is a point that can be added to any of the subject\u2019s Physical or Mental Attributes. There is a risk, however. Compare the total number of successes to the subject\u2019s Stamina. Any excess successes are suffered as bashing damage due to system shock. This damage cannot be soaked. To perform this evocation on another individual, the demonmust be able to make physical contact, and the individual can attempt to counteract its effects -the Storyteller makes a Willpower roll (difficulty 8). </span></span> </div> </div> </div>This power does not state any difficulty, do i go with 6 ?<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>Also for both powers, what is the limit per trait i can raise ? can i raise them up to 10 maximum or ?</b></u>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12206-onedayumay","name":"onedayumay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12206_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T14:31:52-07:00","id":1097296,"title":"","content":"Demon the Fallen questions would get better response in the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness\">Classic World of Darkness forum.</a><br /> <br /> If you ask, a mod might move it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T14:56:31-07:00","id":1097310,"title":"","content":"Alright, can a moderator move this to the appropriate section ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12206-onedayumay","name":"onedayumay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12206_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}